Fixes https://github.com/duckduckgo/autoconsent/issues/333

@muodov this is what you suggested in https://github.com/duckduckgo/autoconsent/issues/333#issuecomment-2330135992 :) I hope I'm getting closer to what you envisioned! I chose the HTML test type instead of JS test as avoiding mocking was very exciting. Let me know if that works for you, as I know you mentioned it as a second option only.

As far as DX goes, I have some reservations (but hopefully they could be addressed in some way) - I'm using Webstorm which has a really nice interface for running tests, but it doesn't work out of the box with the html tests, so it's unusable (maybe with some tweaking and custom run configurations, we could make it work). A bigger nuisance I noticed is that whenever WTR reports any errors, the line numbers don't match - not sure why that is, possibly because we're using esbuild to transform TS into JS ... 🤔 possibly also could be addressed. Last note - when running in `--manual` mode to actually open the test in the browser (which is really handy btw), the first time the html is opened, the browser serves the previously cached version and only upon page refresh it opens the recent one. But maybe the manual mode won't be something we'd use so often.

